thanks for the report

@participant2 could you also start Podman Desktop from the terminal and report the traces you're seeing

`/Applications/Podman\ Desktop.app/Contents/MacOS/Podman\ Desktop`



@reporter 
could you try another thing: If you go to the extensions page (Puzzle icon in navbar, then search for the podman extension and click stop and then start) does it change anything ?


and what is your mac version (not the macOS version) but like is it M1, M2, M3, M4 ?

@participant1 The different podman-desktop releases did not change anything. However, that got me thinking and I believe I've nailed down the issue.

First, I updated podman-desktop back to 1.16.1. Then I went out and looked at podman and noticed that it recently released 5.4.0 2 days ago (around the time I started seeing this issue). So i shut down podman-desktop, uninstalled podman 5.4.0, and installed podman 5.3.2 (the most recent previous version). I then initialized a podman machine and started it from the CLI. When I started up podman-desktop, it deteced the podman machine as expected!

So it appears that some change in the base podman tool has affected how podman-desktop detects the podman machine in the latest podman 5.4.0 release. Not sure if this is a bug in podman 5.4.0 or a change in functionality and a bug in podman-desktop, but I believe this should narrow down where you need to look!

@reporter could you check https://github.com/podman-desktop/prereleases/releases/tag/v1.17.0-202502131559-ee7684367a7

and download a x64 dmg and try it, it's a snapshot release from the current main branch including the fix

direct link: https://github.com/podman-desktop/prereleases/releases/download/v1.17.0-202502131559-ee7684367a7/podman-desktop-1.17.0-202502131559-ee7684367a7-x64.dmg
